zvs|n|A tube, as of cane or reed, sometimes twelve feet long, through which an arrow or other projectile may be impelled by the force of the breath. It is a weapon much used by certain Indians of America and the West Indies; -- called also blowpipe, and blowtube. See Sumpitan.	V:2d6l,81,3~2d6l,81,3	N:68eh,127,4~68eh,127,4
